**Total for the year: €2,120**, so each of you (Sam, Priya and Tom) owes **about €706.67**.

Feb appeared twice in your list (198 both times). I treated that as a typo and counted it once, since a year has 12 months. If there really were two Feb bills, the total would be €2,318 and each share €772.67.

€2,120 doesn't divide evenly by 3, so two people pay €706.67 and one pays €706.66.
